>How is the effectiveness of an item detemined?

DevTeam fiat.  There are essentially three bands of effectiveness:

Band 1 (any monster eligible for offensive items):
  Scroll of earth if wearing a metallic helmet or otherwise liable to have
  their head squashed, otherwise a wand of striking.
  Wand of striking.
  Potion of acid.
  Potion of confusion.
  Potion of blindness.
  Potion of sleeping.
  Potion of paralysis.
  Wand of magic missile. (Twice as likely as the previous entries for
  monsters of difficulty 4 or greater.)

Band 2 (difficulty 7 or greater monsters only):
  Wand of sleep.
  Wand of fire.
  Wand of cold.
  Wand of lightning.

Band 3 (difficulty 8 or greater monsters only):
  Wand of death.

Monsters of difficulty 6 or less get items from band 1; monsters of
difficulty 7 or greater get items from band 1 or 2 (flat distribution
subject to the notes regarding wands of striking and magic missile);
monsters of difficulty 8 or greater have a 1-in-35 chance of getting a
wand of death.

'K', animals, ' ', explosive monsters, and mindless monsters never have
random defensive or offensive items under any circumstances.

